> > {nadyxru facnu}? "hard-to-invert function"
> 
> It's not a {fancu}. Pierre means the functionality of a one-way door, such
> as a trapdoor.

A trapdoor one-way function is indeed a fancu. The classic example is raising 
a variable number (noi cmima lo se fancu) to a fixed power modulo a product of 
large primes, i.e. RSA. If you know the primes, it's easy to calculate the 
inverse function. If you don't, it's computationally infeasible.

